# AWS EC2 Instance Provisioning & Passwordless Root SSH Access

## Project Overview
This project demonstrates automating the deployment of an Amazon EC2 instance (`t2.micro`) named `datacenter-ec2` in the `us-east-1` region using the AWS CLI. It configures secure, passwordless SSH access directly for the `root` user from a designated client host (`aws-client`).

---

## Technical Architecture & Workflow
1. **SSH Key Generation**: Generated a 2048-bit RSA key pair (`/root/.ssh/id_rsa`) on the landing host (`aws-client`).
2. **AWS Key Pair Import**: Imported the public key (`id_rsa.pub`) into AWS EC2 Key Pairs as `datacenter-ec2-key`.
3. **AMI & Instance Provisioning**: Dynamically retrieved the latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI ID and launched a `t2.micro` EC2 instance tagged `Name=datacenter-ec2`.
4. **Security Group Ingress Configuration**: Authorized inbound SSH traffic (TCP port 22) on the instance's primary security group.
5. **Root Access Setup**: Transferred public key credentials to `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` on the target EC2 instance.
6. **Validation**: Verified passwordless SSH access as `root`.

---

## Key Commands Executed

### 1. Key Pair Generation
```bash
sudo mkdir -p /root/.ssh && sudo chmod 700 /root/.ssh
sudo ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 2048 -f /root/.ssh/id_rsa -N ""

2. AWS Key Import & AMI Retrieval


# Import Public Key to AWS
aws ec2 import-key-pair \
  --key-name "datacenter-ec2-key" \
  --public-key-material fileb:///root/.ssh/id_rsa.pub \
  --region us-east-1

# Query Latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI ID
AMI_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-images \
  --owners amazon \
  --filters "Name=name,Values=amzn2-ami-hvm-2.0.*-x86_64-gp2" "Name=state,Values=available" \
  --query "reverse(sort_by(Images, &CreationDate))[0].ImageId" \
  --output text)

3. Instance Deployment & Inbound Security Configuration

# Launch EC2 Instance
INSTANCE_ID=$(aws ec2 run-instances \
  --image-id "$AMI_ID" \
  --instance-type t2.micro \
  --key-name "datacenter-ec2-key" \
  --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=instance,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=datacenter-ec2}]' \
  --query 'Instances[0].InstanceId' \
  --output text)

# Fetch Instance Public IP & Security Group ID
PUBLIC_IP=$(aws ec2 describe-instances --instance-ids "$INSTANCE_ID" --query "Reservations[0].Instances[0].PublicIpAddress" --output text)
SG_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-instances --instance-ids "$INSTANCE_ID" --query "Reservations[0].Instances[0].SecurityGroups[0].GroupId" --output text)

# Authorize Inbound SSH Traffic
aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
  --group-id "$SG_ID" \
  --protocol tcp \
  --port 22 \
  --cidr 0.0.0.0/0

4. Root User Authorization & SSH Verification

# Provision Root authorized_keys File
sudo ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no -i /root/.ssh/id_rsa ec2-user@$PUBLIC_IP \
  "sudo cp /home/ec2-user/.ssh/authorized_keys /root/.ssh/authorized_keys && sudo chown root:root /root/.ssh/authorized_keys"

# Test Passwordless Connection as Root
sudo ssh -i /root/.ssh/id_rsa root@$PUBLIC_IP "hostname"

